[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Start "scandi-nf6 4.c4"]
[Name "4...Nb6: the knight goes wide"]

4... Nb6 { One player in five. The knight hits c4, but it stands away from the king. }
5. Nf3 { The engine prefers this to 5.Nc3, which runs into ...e5. }
5... Bg4 { The most common move. }
6. Be2 e6
7. Nc3 Be7
8. h3 { Asks the bishop what it wants. }
8... Bh5
9. Be3 { The last minor piece comes out and guards d4 and c5. White has the centre and more space. The engine gives nearly a pawn. [%cal Ge3d4] } *
